            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Jurisdiction</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Bhadradri Kothagdem District is named after Bhadrachalamhas famous Sri SeethaRama temple located in Bhadrachalam.This District was newly formed on October 11 2016 during reorganization of Districts.   The district is having large area of forest and most of the population belongs to Tribal’s. Kothagudem is the administrative headquarters of the District.The District is spread over an area of 7,483 square kilometers.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Boundaries of the District</h3>
                    <b>Intrastate</b>
                </div>
                
                <p><b>On South and South East : </b>Khammam District </p><br>
                <p><b>On West		   :</b>Mahabubabad District </p><br>
                <p><b>North West			:</b> JayasankarBhupalpallyDistrict</p>
                <br>
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <b>Interstate</b>
                </div>
                <p><b>East : </b>Khammam District </p><br>
                <p><b>North and North east	   :</b>Bijapur and Sukma Districts of Chhattisgarh state</p><br>
                <p><b>South East :</b>West Godavari District.</p>

            </div>
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Demography of the District</h3>
                </div>
                <p>According to 2011 census, the district has population of 12,13,987 of which Female 6,10,454 and Male 6,03,533.Population density of 197 person/sq.km. It has sex ratio of 1008 and literacy rate of 66.40%.People belonging to various communities live in harmony. Majority of the Population consists of Tribal’s in the District.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Socio Economic Cultural peculiarity of the district</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Entire district comes under Tribal Sub - plan. 4 out of 5 Assembly constituencies are reserved for ST. The Rural-Urban ratio is pegged at 70: 30</p>
                <br>
                <p>                                     The District is having Tribal population in large number. Koyas, Lambadas and Kodareddies are accommodated in the District.  Majority of Tribal’s are from Koyacommunity followed by Lambadas. Whereas Konda Reddies belongs to primitive tribal groups lives on the hillocks of some pockets of the district.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Administrative set up of the district</h3>
                </div>
                <p>BhadradriKothagudem District comprises of (2) Revenue Divisions i.e., Bhadrachalam and Kothagudem with (23) Mandals, (479) Gram Panchayats and (377) Revenue Villages.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Roads & Transport</h3>
                </div>
                <p>Bhadradri Kothagudem district head quarte is well concted through Bhadrachalam Road Railway station from South Central Railways (Secunderabad) and there are TSRTC and APSRTC Bus services from Kothagudem to all important towns and other neibhourDistrictsand States. District head quarter is located 280 Kms from Hyderabad via Khammam.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Education</h3>
                </div>
                <p>The University College of Engineering Kakatiya University formally known as the Kothagudem School of Mines(KSM) is first mining college in Telanagana State and Second in India</p>
            </div>
            <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Industries</h3>
                </div>
                <p> <b>Singareni Collieries</b> The district is endowed with a variety of important minerals such as Coal. The Singareni Collieries Company Limited (SCCL), a Government coal mining company jointly owned by the Government of Telangana and Government of India, has its headquarters in Kothagudem. SCCL is currently operating 16 opencast and 30 underground mines in (10) districts of Telangana with manpower around 58,837. </p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Kothagudem Thermal Power Station</b>is located in Paloncha is one of the coal based power plants of Telangana Power Generation Corporation Limited (TSGENCO).Heavy Water Plant is located in Aswapuram mandal of Pinaka Constituency of BhadradriKothagudem and it is first in Asia.</p>
                <br>
                
                <p><b>ITC- Paperboards </b>and Specialty Papers Division (ITC-PSPD) which is amongst the leading names in the business worldwide is located at Sarapaka village near BhadrachalamKothagudem district is also rich in forest reserves.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="contentSectionDiv" align="justify">
                <div class="contentSectionHeading">
                    <h3>Place of Interest</h3>
                </div>
                <p><b>Bhadrachalam</b>, a key town of pilgrimage importance is located in Kothagudem district. The temple town of Bhadrachalam is situated on the bank of Godavari River. The town shares its historical significance with Ramayana Era. The name Bhadrachalam is derived from the word Bhadragiri (The Mountain Abode of Bhadra, the child of Meru and Menaka). The famous temple at Bhadrachalam is home to the ArchaMurthys of Rama, Sita and Lakshmana and their idols are believed to be swayambhu i.e., self-manifested ones.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>The Kinnerasani project </b> or the Dam is a storage reservoir constructed on the Kinnerasani River in the Godavari Basin at Yanambail village of Palvoncha Mandal. Kinnerasani River is an important tributary of the river Godavari. The scenic beauty created by the landscape along the Kinnerasani River is a panoramic one abutted by lush green landscape. The Kinnerasani sanctuary, a part of the Dandakaranya Forests, is a haven of exotic wildlife and tourists enjoy their visit here by spotting several animals in their natural habitat.</p>
                <br>
                <p><b>Parnashala</b>, a popular tourist place, is a village in the Dummugudem Mandal. It is said to be the place where the evil-minded king Ravana abducted Goddess Sita. This place unfolds this part of the epic Ramayana by exhibiting the primary events with beautifully canvassed sculptures of Shri Ram, Sita, Laxmana, and Ravan.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
